cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its experimental records, please cite both the software (this file) and the accompanying paper (preferred-citation below)."
title: "LifeEngine: a preregistered agent-based apparatus for testing persistence of developmental differences and reuse of experience"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-22
# Dual licensed. CFF permits a list; the first entry, Apache-2.0, applies to the
# repository as a whole and is the less permissive of the two. Documentation,
# preregistration texts, and result data are additionally available under
# CC BY 4.0. See LICENSE, LICENSE-DOCS.md and NOTICE for the file-by-file split.
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A pure-Python, zero-LLM, dependency-free artificial-life agent-based model
  built as a minimal apparatus for one question: do different experiences
  during a developmental period still leave a difference after an agent is
  transplanted into an identical environment, and can those differences be put
  to use on an unfamiliar new problem? The repository contains the model core,
  two byte-frozen model versions with SHA-256 manifests, the preregistration
  texts and amendments for every confirmatory experiment, a non-recyclable
  random-seed ledger, one-shot confirmation runners with crash-safe burn locks,
  and the verbatim result records of experiments 025 and 027-029, including
  conclusions later withdrawn.
authors:
  - family-names: Qin
    given-names: Yinan
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4448-3969"
keywords:
  - artificial life
  - agent-based modeling
  - developmental plasticity
  - path dependence
  - common-garden design
  - preregistration
  - individual differences
  - experience transfer
  - relational memory structure
  - agent memory architecture
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "Preregistration for Experiment 029 (relational-memory transfer)"
    notes: >-
      Authoritative Chinese original, released unmodified as
      docs/MEMORY_TRANSFER029_PREREGISTRATION.md. Its SHA-256 is
      29e45930a07f2649c7958fdc0cd20a389005ca43e93287b9f69e2ccdcf867145,
      which is the value frozen in final_029.py and independently recomputed
      by tools/verify_provenance.py.
    authors:
      - family-names: Qin
        given-names: Yinan
